import java.util.Stack;

public class MinimumInsertion {
    /**
     * Calculates the minimum number of insertions required to make the string balanced.
     * 
     * @param s The input string containing only '(' and ')' characters.
     * @return The minimum number of insertions required.
     */
    public int minInsertions(String s) {
        Stack<Character> stack = new Stack<>();
        int balance = 0;
        int insertions = 0;

        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') {
                stack.push(c);
            } else {
                if (stack.isEmpty()) {
                    balance++;
                    insertions++;
                } else {
                    stack.pop();
                }
            }
        }

        int missingLeft = balance;
        insertions += missingLeft;

        return insertions;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        MinimumInsertion minInsert = new MinimumInsertion();

        // Test cases
        String test1 = "(()))";
        System.out.println(minInsert.minInsertions(test1)); // Expected output: 1

        String test2 = "((()))";
        System.out.println(minInsert.minInsertions(test2)); // Expected output: 0
    }
}
```

The `minInsertions` method uses a `Stack` to keep track of the opening parentheses. It iterates through the characters of the input string, balancing the count of opening and closing parentheses. If the stack becomes empty, it means the current closing parenthesis does not have a matching opening parenthesis, so an insertion is needed. The minimum number of insertions required to make the string balanced is the sum of the missing opening parentheses.

